                <pb facs="0928" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/950a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-21T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>68. For McIlhenny.</p>
                <p>Department is advised that interest on foreign debt has not been paid since
                    January. Please advise Department whether interest now due can be paid from
                    available surplus on hand and if so inform Department of the reasons for the
                    non-payment of interest. Repeated inquiries on this subject have been addressed
                    to the Department by the French Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
